    "whyPromptsWork": "Every prompt asks for what the photo *doesn't* show — sound, off-camera story, background detail, what happened on the way there. That gap is where the real memory lives. “Nearly deleted” and “ordinary day” prompts are the strongest — they sacralize the unremarkable.",
    "playWhen": "Long-distance or after time apart. Pair with Photo Flashback — Receipts is race + story, Flashback is dual captions.",
    "makeItLand": "Let the photo-finder tell first. Don't correct their version — add yours. **Watch out:** Skip photos tied to a painful memory unless both partners want to go there.",
    "watchOut": "Skip photos tied to a painful memory unless both partners want to go there.",
